### How many full years had elapsed between Nigeria's independence date and October 1, 2020?
Answer: Based on the search result, Nigeria gained independence on **October 1, 1960**. The claim is dated **October 1, 2020**, which means exactly **60 full years** had elapsed between Nigeria's independence date and the date of the claim. This is also consistent with the claim itself, which refers to "Nigeria's 60 years of existence as a nation."

Source URL: https://www.blackpast.org/global-african-history/1957-alhaji-abubakar-tafawa-balewa-unity-and-diversity-independence/

### What were the start and end dates of the first military government in Nigeria following the January 1966 coup that overthrew the First Republic?
Answer: The first military government in Nigeria began on January 15, 1966, following the coup that overthrew the First Republic, and ended approximately six months later in July 1966 after a counter-coup.

Source URL: https://www.bbc.com/news/world-africa-35312370

