### What were the start and end dates of the military government led by General Sani Abacha, and what was the duration of the transitional military government led by General Abdulsalami Abubakar that followed it until Nigeria's return to civilian rule in May 1999?
Answer: General Sani Abacha's military rule lasted from November 1993, when he took power, until his sudden death in June 1998. The transitional military government led by General Abdulsalami Abubakar lasted from June 1998 until the handover to civilian rule on May 29, 1999, a period of approximately eleven months.

